{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\n// Method on Validator<D>.\n/// Encode the answer and atomically replace this source/criterion's record.\npub fn store_evidence<O: serde::Serialize>(\n    &self,\n    inputs: &Fingerprinted<D, O>,\n) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n```\n\nThe method saves under the source identity and criterion path captured in\n`Fingerprinted`, preserving its revision, input trace, and completed answer. Encoding follows\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output`; atomic replacement follows\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage`. The result type needs\nno `Sync` bound: the method encodes the answer and captures the record and\nstorage key before constructing the storage future.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately cover `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.store_evidence`.\n\nObligations and the tests that cover them:\n\n- **Save under the captured source identity and criterion path.**\n  - `contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` stores a verified value and reloads it. The loaded value keeps the same source node id and criterion path.\n  - The same test stores three criteria (`behavior`, `structure`, `text`) and finds each record under its own criterion path.\n  - `agent.rs#fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]` asserts that the stored record is keyed by node 1.\n  - `contracts.rs#fn[concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records]` loads the stored record by `(Node(1), [\"behavior\"])`.\n\n- **Preserve revision, input trace and completed answer.**\n  - The `criteria_keep_typed_answers…` test asserts that revision, dependencies and output survive the round trip. The raw stored output is checked as JSON.\n  - Its dependencies are empty, but other tests cover non-empty ones:\n    - The concurrent test asserts the saved revision and the saved `Dependency::Node` fingerprint.\n    - `input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations` asserts the stored dependencies after a replacement.\n    - The edge-selection agent test asserts the stored `OutgoingEdges` dependency.\n    - `validation.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` asserts the stored `Node` dependency.\n\n- **Atomic replacement of the source/criterion record.**\n  - `input_checking…` persists an old record and then a new one. It asserts that the stored dependencies are the new ones.\n  - `typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence` replaces a v1 record and asserts `records.len()==1`.\n  - The concurrent test saves two competing records for the same key. It asserts that one complete record remains, with its revision, dependencies and output all coming from the same save.\n  - The `criteria_keep_typed_answers…` test checks that `verify` does not write. A save is needed before a record exists, and a save of a different value is needed to replace it.\n\n- **Encoding follows `record.output` (cited).**\n  - `serialization_failure_leaves_the_existing_record_unchanged` uses an `Unencodable` answer. It expects `ValidationError::Output`. It then asserts that the old record's revision, dependencies and output are unchanged and that the write count is still 1.\n  - `resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments` sets `fail_store` and expects `ValidationError::Graph(\"store\")`. It asserts that no record is written.\n  - `storage.rs#fn[malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors]` stores through a file-backed store.\n\n- **No `Sync` bound on the result.** `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` stores a `Cell<u32>` answer, which is `Send` but not `Sync`. It passes the store future through `send<T: Send>`, which enforces the `Send` bound at compile time. It then loads the value back and asserts that the output is 17.\n\nI found no untested obligation, and no `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "c5be9371a473ffa255255c022bb11420323a182274572f2d2b5dcf8a8460fd07",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.store_evidence",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.store_evidence"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} store_evidence",
        "```rust,ignore",
        "// Method on Validator<D>.",
        "/// Encode the answer and atomically replace this source/criterion's record.",
        "pub fn store_evidence<O: serde::Serialize>(",
        "    &self,",
        "    inputs: &Fingerprinted<D, O>,",
        ") -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;",
        "```",
        "",
        "The method saves under the source identity and criterion path captured in",
        "`Fingerprinted`, preserving its revision, input trace, and completed answer. Encoding follows",
        "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output`; atomic replacement follows",
        "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage`. The result type needs",
        "no `Sync` bound: the method encodes the answer and captures the record and",
        "storage key before constructing the storage future.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} record.output",
        "`Validator::store_evidence` serializes the answer in `Fingerprinted` before passing",
        "the complete record to storage. A serialization failure returns",
        "`ValidationError::Output` and leaves the existing record unchanged. A storage",
        "failure returns `ValidationError::Graph`.",
        "",
        "`Validator::load_evidence` decodes a loaded record's output into the requested",
        "`Criterion::Ok`. An output that cannot decode returns `ValidationError::Output`,",
        "including when the saved revision or inputs are stale. Missing evidence returns",
        "`Ok(None)`; malformed stored records and storage failures return",
        "`ValidationError::Graph`. Revision and input comparison belong to the caller's",
        "reuse workflow under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.procedure_identity`.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} evidence_storage",
        "```rust,ignore",
        "use std::future::Future;",
        "",
        "// Defined in habeas_sdk::graph.",
        "pub trait Storage: Graph {",
        "    /// Ok(None) means absent; Err means loading failed.",
        "    fn load_evidence(",
        "        &self,",
        "        source: &Self::NodeId,",
        "        criterion: &CriterionPath,",
        "    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<",
        "        Option<Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>>,",
        "        Self::Error,",
        "    >> + Send;",
        "",
        "    /// Atomically replace only this source/criterion pair's complete record.",
        "    fn store_evidence(",
        "        &self,",
        "        source: &Self::NodeId,",
        "        criterion: &CriterionPath,",
        "        record: &Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>,",
        "    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send;",
        "}",
        "```",
        "",
        "The validator passes the source identity and criterion path to both methods. The",
        "key preserves both parts: source paths `[\"a\"]` and `[\"a\", \"b\"]` with criteria",
        "`[\"b\", \"c\"]` and `[\"c\"]` identify different records, even though flattening each",
        "pair would produce the same segments.",
        "",
        "Different criteria of a source have independent records. A revision change",
        "invalidates the same criterion's record rather than creating another key.",
        "The interface requires neither filesystem paths nor global evidence listing.",
        "",
        "Successful loads observe either an old or new complete record, or absence",
        "before the first save. Successful competing saves leave one complete record;",
        "its revision, dependencies, and output all belong to that save. No ordering",
        "between competing saves is guaranteed.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
